y": 153, "tool_args": {"stage": "experienced", "strategy": "rv_parks", "parent_strategy": "commercial"}, "voice_bridge": "You need both a resource and a vendor connection. Here is what I would do.", "is_active": true, "created_at": "2026-06-09T22:05:14.41674+00:00", "notes": null}, {"id": "4e5a4d35-e48f-42ef-95d1-710292614552", "rule_name": "Commercial - RV Parks - Veteran", "stage_key": "veteran", "strategy": "rv_parks", "blocker": null, "path": "B", "routing_action": "getEducationMatch", "tier": "2_and_3", "priority": 154, "tool_args": {"stage": "veteran", "strategy": "rv_parks", "parent_strategy": "commercial"}, "voice_bridge": "You need both a resource and a vendor connection. Here is what I would do.", "is_active": true, "created_at": "2026-06-09T22:05:14.41674+00:00", "notes": null}, {"id": "189c7f89-f496-47d5-9980-435714c1eb61", "rule_name": "Passive Investing - Deals (not Deal Center)", "stage_key": null, "strategy": "passive_investing", "blocker": "deals", "path": "both", "routing_action": "getVendorMatch", "tier": "2_vendor", "priority": 5, "tool_args": null, "voice_bridge": "Our Deal Center listings are active deals, so they are not really a passive fit. The closest thing we have is the True Wealth Joint Venture Club, where members take down deals together. It is free to join, and once a deal comes together there are legal, bookkeeping and tax costs that usually come out of the investment. Worth knowing it is an active club rather than fully passive.", "is_active": true, "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:41:18.534325+00:00", "notes": "Added 2026-09-27 after a live call. Chris: EVERYTHING IN DEAL CENTER IS MEANT FOR ACTIVE INVESTORS, so routing a passive investor there makes no sense. The broad rule \"Property Listings - Deals Blocker\" (priority 10, strategy NULL, path both) was matching passive_investing callers and offering them active-deal inventory. The correct rule \"Active - Passive Investing\" sits at priority 73 and never got a chance, because lower priority wins. THIS RULE IS PRIORITY 5 so it beats the Deal Center rule, while leaving that rule broad for every other strategy, which is what Chris asked for. path=both to match the rule it must outrank. True Wealth is the closest fit and the voice_bridge says so honestly, including that it is NOT fully passive and that deal-level costs apply (the mandatory framing from item 43 / reia_resources)."}]$v1snap$);

